Endless Sky is pretty much Escape Velocity with a new universe and a lot of QoL fixes. It's a 2d space exploration and fighting game that is quite heavily story driven. Outside of the story, you can't do much more than get the best ship you can and crush everything with your fleet.
PROS:
- The story is quite good (only if you like reading though, it's all text) and more is being added;
- Universe is interesting, but nothing groundbreaking;
- There's quite a lot of ship and fleet progression to go through before you can kill almost anyone;
- UI is simple but works well (especially compared to EV).
CONs:
- The combat is pretty bland, whoever has better ship/larger fleet will win with few exceptions;
- Story is lacking in actual interesting gameplay, especially if you heavily overpower what it expects you to have (the gap between your possible power levels is immense);
- Making money through plundering is too easy - with huge fleets of pirates you don't even need to kill yourself to plunder;
- You can abandon story quests after which you can't pick them up again. :)
For me personally, 100+ hours of gameplay I enjoyed for free is a definite recommend. However, this is a very nostalgic game - X3 Albion Prelude would work better for someone who is not a fan of 2d combat and text story.

